  "caveats": [
    "Real landforms also contribute power to the amplitude spectrum, so the null field contains their power redistributed as incoherent texture; the null therefore OVERESTIMATES the pure-artifact pit count and is an upper bound, not an estimate, of the artifact contribution.",
    "Phase randomization destroys the spatial phase-coherence of the row banding; the null's trough-association rate is measured against each null field's own band field and is reported for comparison with the observed 61.2% trough association, not as a direct replication of it.",
    "The taper suppresses power within ~30 px of nodata edges before the FFT; variance is restored globally by rescaling, so the null is slightly smoother near mask edges than the real field."
